WEBVTT

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:06.980
Hey, Kaito!

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.730
What is the story behind Jin Makata?

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.660
What are his connections with 
that Master Brain freak?

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.020
Hey!

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:22.470
We nearly got killed by 
some Master Brain who

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.940
was fulfillin’ Jin Makata’s wishes!

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.320
Jin doesn’t have 
anything to do with them!

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>Menacing figure detected.</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:30.250
What?

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.120
<i>Menacing figure detected.</i>

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.460
Iwashimizu, Gammon isn’t 
a “menacing figure.”

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:44.590
Hey, Cubik! Is Iwashimizu 
missing a screw or two?

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:47.310
I don’t think so...

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.690
Jin-Jin?

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.000
Even So, I Believe in Him

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.260
These are hard to carry...
 And I can barely see...

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.280
Huh?

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.280
Are you all right?

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.780
Jin?!

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.360
Th-thank you!

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.900
My teacher asked me to carry these...

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.230
It was nothing.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.200
Carrying all of these must be tough.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.450
Let me help.

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.160
I can handle it!

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.520
Believe it or not, I’m pretty strong.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:20.830
Sweet!

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:27.420
These are hard to carry...
 And I can barely see...

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:33.100
Huh?

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.510
Hello.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.230
“Jin Makata has nothing to 
do with that organization.”

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.870
What makes you say that?

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.770
I know Jin.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:51.860
If I said he’s got nothing to do 
with them, that’s the way it is.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.550
I figured you were gonna say that.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.880
I’ll ask the guy in question!

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.120
What?! Gammon, you jerk!

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.330
Wanna fight, DaiMORON?! 
Hey! Guys, you need to calm down!

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:03.830
What are you doing?

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.080
<i>Suspicious character detected.</i>

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.210
She transferred to our school.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:11.640
Raetsel!

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:15.260
Hi there.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:21.150
I don’t see any reason 
to reject your application.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:27.900
I appreciate how quickly you accepted 
it, Principal Baron Kaidou.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.370
I couldn’t sit on a personal request

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.070
made by President Enigma 
of the Republic of Amgine.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.790
I don’t care about that sorta stuff.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.800
Then allow me to ask you something 
as the principal of this school.

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.620
What brought you to Root Gakuen?

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:47.800
I came... because Jin lacks something.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:49.840
What might that be?

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:52.340
Me!

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:57.860
Mr. Takeda! She’s a first 
year high school student!

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.550
A first year, huh?

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:03.890
Not to brag, but aren’t all of the 
ladies who transfer here beautiful?

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:06.520
Yep! Good job, Principal!

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.400
Oh, I’ve got it!

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.690
For the next school festival, 
what do you think of making

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:14.830
“Root Gakuen’s Survival 
of the Hottest Puzzle”?

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:19.070
The title alone sounds 
exciting, Mr. Takeda!

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.210
Doesn’t it, Mr. Aizawa?

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.050
Hello there, Raetsel.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.180
Hello!

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.190
Hello.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.470
I’m Student Council 
President Tamaki Chieno.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.880
If you have any questions 
about Root Gakuen,

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:45.470
please feel free to ask.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:47.200
I’m Erena Himekawa.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.940
You’re a Giver, aren’t you?

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:51.410
Yes.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.860
I’m amazed you could tell, Miss Erena.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:57.250
My intuition as a fellow Giver told 
me, Student Council President!

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.570
I’m Airi Mizutani.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.450
Would you be interested in 
joining the Puzzle Club?

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:03.550
The Puzzle Club?

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:07.290
This is called the “Licky-Licky 
Bucket Puzzle.”

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.920
I made it!

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:16.810
You win if you can fit all six 
Licky-Licky’s in the bucket and close the lid,

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.900
but... to be honest... 
even I can’t solve it!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.050
L-Licky-Lacky? Drippy-Droppy?

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.790
Licky-Licky!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.450
Nice to meet you, Miss Raetsel!

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.710
Sheesh! Why did I have 
to carry those boxes?!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.020
Jin Makata!

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.540
Ain’t he buds with the principal?

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.880
So why’s he hiding?

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:15.730
What?!

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:01.820
Jin...

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.410
What’re you after?

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.750
Lady, you’ve got something 
up your sleeve, don’t you?

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.750
You even took the trouble 
to transfer to our school...

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.080
Wait!

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:16.420
I won’t let you escape!

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.130
You can’t trick me.

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:23.550
Is he--Jin Makata--

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.550
an angel who loves puzzles?

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:30.030
Or is he a demon who hates them?!

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.330
So, you’re not sure

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:35.030
if you should take Kaito 
Daimon’s word at face value.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:38.980
Jin despises puzzles.

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:40.570
He hates them with all his heart.

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.690
You’ll have to decide 
for yourself whether

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.940
you’ll take my word 
for it or Kaito’s.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.030
Gammon!

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:51.980
What’re you doing to that girl?!

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:56.710
Raetsel, you...!

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:00.430
Don’t worry. I won’t 
do anything to Jin.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:02.920
I said I’d let you watch 
over him, didn’t I?

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:05.090
I’m rather curious, you know.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:09.340
Are you capable of helping Jin 
regain his memories or not?

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.930
I think that girl is in love...

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:14.180
In love...?

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.680
When it comes to that chick, 
that kind of naïve

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:18.950
thinking will get you hurt!

00:09:19.270 --> 00:09:21.910
They’re hiding something.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:26.330
And by “they,” I mean 
Raetsel and Jin Makata.

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.700
Jin isn’t that type of guy!

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.340
So everything they’ve 
said is a lie? Seriously?!

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:33.640
Jin would never do the 
crap they’ve claimed!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:36.040
Kaito Daimon, I shall take advantage 
of your deep sense of trust.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.240
Oh, right!

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.290
And I’m supposed to believe 
everything you say about him.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:38.970
You musta stuck to Jin like glue!

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:55.740
Jin made me realize that 
puzzles aren’t my enemies.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:10:00.530
He taught me that 
puzzles are my friends.

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:05.230
After a Puzzle of Fools 
killed my parents,

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:08.450
my heart had grown dark and cold.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:14.620
But Jin and his puzzles warmed 
my heart, thawing the ice...

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:24.560
Meeting a puzzle is the 
same as meeting a person.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.420
Solve them. Set them free.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.630
Free the puzzles.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:32.090
The puzzles have done nothing wrong.

00:10:32.890 --> 00:10:35.350
The blame should fall 
on those who made them.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:39.730
Never lose sight of 
what matters... never!

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:47.090
Aw, you hit another dead end!

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.520
At this rate, I’ll 
never reach the goal!

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.670
If you do this, it opens up a new path!

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.410
You’re doing great!

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:04.540
If you run into a wall, you 
can always make a new path.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:08.110
There is no path you can’t make...

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.040
in both puzzles and in life!

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:18.110
There is no way Jin 
could hate puzzles...!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:27.460
<i>Menacing figure approaching.</i>

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.210
What’s wrong, Iwashimizu?

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:36.630
Can you hear me, Kaito?

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:37.550
Jin!

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.920
It has the Republic of 
Amgine’s coat of arms!

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.680
Face me via a puzzle!

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.940
What are you going to do, Kaito?

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.440
Stop where you stand, DaiMORON!

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.310
Kaito!

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.770
Wait for me!

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:52.690
Please wait up!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:53.690
Kaito!

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:07.540
I see you didn’t chicken out, Kaito!

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:12.040
Just what I would expect from my pupil.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.210
What’s wrong?

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:16.960
Have I managed to shock you speechless?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:21.090
Jin, have your memories come back?

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:26.810
Yeah! That is precisely why I 
am standing here before you.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:34.440
I will use puzzles to destroy 
the Phi-Brain children.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:40.280
Kaito, consider it an 
honor to fall by my hand!

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:41.490
It can’t be...

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:43.650
Jin, you would never...!

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.660
No way... This can’t be right!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.290
This is a dream! It’s all an illusion!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.000
Kaito...

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.380
This is a lie!

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.260
Please tell me that 
this is all a lie, Jin!

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.430
Just kidding!

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:08.550
What?!

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:13.480
I know that you’re not the real Jin!

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.020
He’s not Jin...?

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.230
I think he’s an imposter.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.250
M-me, an imposter?

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:33.460
What are you talking about?

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.750
Cut the crap!

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:41.030
Are you the Jin that those Master 
Brain guys keep talking about?

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:44.760
It would be an honor if 
that’s what you thought.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:48.310
That man is my treasure.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:50.770
You--!

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.010
That jerk!

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:56.070
Master Jin Makata,

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:59.740
I revere you as my one and 
only teacher in the world.

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.360
Keeping my pledge to you,

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.280
I have sworn to annihilate 
the puzzlers of the world!

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:09.040
I have dedicated my 
heart and soul to you!

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:13.120
I am the most ingenious 
Master Brain Giver!

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.250
My name is none other than Jin Masaka!

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.000
Masaka?!

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:21.250
So it musta been you who stuck 
out your tongue back there...

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:25.800
Master Jin Makata, to 
think that I’ll get to

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.960
defeat Kaito Daimon in front of you...

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:31.390
Nothing could fill me with greater joy.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:36.230
Please watch this battle 
through to the end!

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:37.940
Knock it off, Fake!

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:41.730
I’ll solve your puzzle 
in three seconds.

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.200
Sounds promising!

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.740
In that case, pick up that controller.

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:55.990
This massive puzzle is a sliding 
puzzle combined together with a maze.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:03.130
You’re supposed to race toward 
the goal on the opposite end

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.880
while using the controller 
to move the blocks.

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:09.630
However, if you fail to reach the 
goal within the time limit...

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:11.640
What will happen?

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:13.010
You’ll fall!

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:26.070
Puzzle time... Let's begin!

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:31.450
Wait!

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.870
So this is the entrance.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:37.330
Let’s see...

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:13.370
Even if you know how to solve 
it, can you get out in time?

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:27.800
He’s having a rough time...

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:30.010
Don’t let that fake beat you, Kaito!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.300
But...

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:33.600
He may be a phony,

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.730
but what if he’s perfectly copying

00:16:35.730 --> 00:16:39.520
Jin Makata’s appearance along 
with his skill with puzzles?

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:41.140
That’s not possible!

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.630
This is pretty good for 
an imposter’s puzzle!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.920
You won’t be making 
wise cracks for long!

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.180
I need more time!

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:32.650
It looks like he’s 
taking a roundabout path.

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:34.870
Nope, he’s doin’ good.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.290
Huh? But...

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:40.460
Kaito has caught on, but...

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:43.040
Simply sliding the blocks 
wouldn’t be that bad,

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:47.550
but the intricate maze inside 
makes this way too complex.

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:51.260
And that isn’t everything.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:53.050
He’s hiding something up his sleeve.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:17:59.050
Looks like I’m gonna make it!

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:03.060
Not happening!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.540
I knew you were an imposter!

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.910
Jin would never pull a 
cowardly stunt like that!

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:27.460
You’re wrong! That was 
by no means cowardly!

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:30.420
“Do whatever it takes to win!”

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.920
That was one of Master 
Jin Makata’s teachings!

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:36.420
The bastard!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:44.470
Got it!

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:55.190
I’ll just have to sharpen the slope!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.270
Kaito!

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:27.680
Will I make it?

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:06.230
I made it...

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:07.270
Yay!

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.940
Whoa, hey! Don’t! 
Yay!

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:11.390
Kaito, you made it!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.900
I’d expect no less from my Kaito.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:21.410
N-no way! And I came so close...!

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:26.620
I never expected him to defeat 
me, the great Jin Masaka...

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:30.560
Wait!

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:57.320
Kaito, it’s not like I don’t 
get how you feel about Jin Makata.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:02.120
On the other hand, not only has 
Raetsel transferred to our school,

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.610
but we’ve also had a Jin 
Makata imposter pop up.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.750
This is serious business!

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:08.620
What are you going to do?

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:12.120
If Master Brains start attacking 
one after the next...?

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:14.800
Bring them on! I’ll take ’em down!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:20.130
No, I will solve all of the puzzles.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:21.390
No, I will!

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:22.050
I will!

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:23.180
I said I will!

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:25.010
Did something happen 
to get you worked up?

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:25.350
Just a minute ago--
I can’t tell you!

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:27.720
Now, now. Let’s stop right there.

00:21:38.860 --> 00:21:42.450
What was the point of 
that puzzle battle?

00:21:44.280 --> 00:21:46.820
Now, now. Don’t get so upset.

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:52.250
It is not as though I keep tabs 
on each and every Master Brain.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.210
I will defeat Kaito Daimon!

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:58.210
That was our agreement!

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:00.530
I hope you do.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.510
Oh, pardon me.

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:09.020
I simply meant that I hope you 
have not lost the will to fight

00:22:09.020 --> 00:22:12.010
now that you are with Jin Makata.

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:15.730
I might...

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:18.280
Oh, dear! I hope that was a joke.

00:22:18.730 --> 00:22:19.730
Back at you.

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:24.740
You’re such a naughty 
kitten, teasing an adult.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.970
Now then, let’s get 
the barbeque under way!

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:08.010
Cook the meat and onions uniformly.

00:24:08.010 --> 00:24:11.100
Sure thing! There, 
there, there and there!

00:24:12.100 --> 00:24:14.430
You want your kabobs perfect and fast?!

00:24:14.430 --> 00:24:17.190
Go, Gammon! Make the next one.

00:24:17.190 --> 00:24:21.230
Next time: A Good Meal 
can Resolve Most Problems

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:27.970
A Good Meal can Resolve Most Problems

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:24.270
How am I supposed to 
make this, Principal?!

00:24:24.610 --> 00:24:26.270
There, there and there!

